    {
      "source": "The key-value abstraction within Spring Data Key Value requires an <code>Adapter</code> that shields the native store implementation, freeing up <code>KeyValueTemplate</code> to work on top of any key-value pair-like structure.\nKeys are distributed across <a href=\"#key-value.keyspaces\">Keyspaces</a>.\nUnless otherwise specified, the class name is used as the default keyspace for an entity.\nThe following interface definition shows the <code>KeyValueOperations</code> interface, which is the heart of Spring Data Key-Value:",
      "translation": "Spring Data Key Value 中的键值抽象需要一个 `<code>Adapter`</code>，该适配器屏蔽了原生存储实现，从而让 `<code>KeyValueTemplate`</code> 能够基于任何类似键值对的结构进行工作。  \n键分布在<a href=\"#key-value.keyspaces\">命名空间</a>中。  \n除非另有说明，否则类的名称将用作实体的默认命名空间。  \n以下接口定义展示了 `<code>KeyValueOperations`</code> 接口，它是 Spring Data Key-Value 的核心：",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "Spring Data KeyValue provides easy configuration and access to <code>Map</code> like structures that associate values with unique keys.\nIt offers both low-level and high-level abstractions for interacting with the underlying data structure, freeing the user from infrastructural concerns.",
      "translation": "Spring Data KeyValue 提供了便捷的配置方式，用于访问将值与唯一键关联的类似 <code>Map</code> 的结构。它同时提供低级和高级抽象来与底层数据结构交互，使用户无需关注基础设施细节。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "Keyspaces define the part of the data structure in which the entity should be kept.\nThis concept is similar to collections in MongoDB and Elasticsearch, cores in Solr, and tables in JPA.\nBy default, the keyspace of an entity is extracted from its type, but you can also store entities of different types within one keyspace.",
      "translation": "Keyspaces 定义了实体应存储的数据结构部分。  \n这一概念类似于 MongoDB 和 Elasticsearch 中的集合、Solr 中的核心以及 JPA 中的表。  \n默认情况下，实体的键空间是从其类型中提取的，但您也可以将不同类型的实体存储在同一个键空间中。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
